{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --untracked-files=all && git diff --check && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added IF/ID opcode decoding in `hazard_unit.sv`. The load-use interlock\n  compares rs1 for R-type, OP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR opcodes,\n  and rs2 for R-type, STORE, and BRANCH opcodes. The existing nonzero-rd\n  check and stall/flush priority logic are unchanged.\n- Passed the IF/ID opcode into the hazard unit from `core.sv`.\n- Added retirement-time register-file read ports for RVFI rs1/rs2 data.\n  RVFI source addresses remain unchanged, including raw fields for\n  instructions that do not architecturally read those fields.\n\n## Deviations and rationale\n\nThe initial source-use change exposed a mismatch between the core's raw\nRVFI source-address convention and the register values captured at decode:\nformal checks those raw addresses even for instructions without register\nsources. Retirement-time reads keep those RVFI data fields consistent with\nthe architectural register state without restoring false load-use bubbles.\nThese added reads only feed RVFI outputs and are pruned from the timed\nmemory-side netlist.\n\nNo tests or files outside `cores/bench/rtl/` were changed.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=20 bash\n  formal/run_all.sh`): pass, 53 passed and 0 failed. An earlier run exposed\n  the raw-source-field issue described above; the final RTL passes.\n- Cosim (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): pass, both ELF checks passed.\n  The bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults to `NRET=2` in this checkout\n  and cannot build this `nret: 1` core, so the declared width was supplied.\n\n## Concerns\n\nThe extra register-file read ports add verification-side logic, but they\nfeed only RVFI fields and are not expected to affect FPGA timing or area\nafter synthesis pruning.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
