{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && git diff -- cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv && sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ndiff --git a/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv b/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\nindex c488084..146903b 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n@@ -22,6 +22,16 @@ module alu (\n \n   logic        [4:0]  shamt;\n \n+  // Four 8-bit carry-select slices for the ADD operation. Each upper\n+  // slice computes both possible sums in parallel; only the carry choice\n+  // crosses a slice boundary.\n+  logic [8:0] add_low;\n+  logic [8:0] add1_c0, add1_c1, add1_selected;\n+  logic [8:0] add2_c0, add2_c1, add2_selected;\n+  logic [7:0] add3_c0, add3_c1;\n+  logic       add_c8, add_c16, add_c24;\n+  logic [31:0] add_result;\n+\n   // 64-bit products, computed once and selected per op.\n   // mul_ss/mul_su low halves are unused (only MULH/MULHSU read the high\n   // half). Verilator's UNUSEDSIGNAL is silenced locally — the unused\n@@ -35,12 +45,30 @@ module alu (\n   always_comb begin\n     shamt = b[4:0];\n \n+    add_low = {1'b0, a[7:0]} + {1'b0, b[7:0]};\n+    add_c8  = add_low[8];\n+\n+    add1_c0       = {1'b0, a[15:8]} + {1'b0, b[15:8]};\n+    add1_c1       = {1'b0, a[15:8]} + {1'b0, b[15:8]} + 9'd1;\n+    add1_selected = add_c8 ? add1_c1 : add1_c0;\n+    add_c16       = add1_selected[8];\n+\n+    add2_c0       = {1'b0, a[23:16]} + {1'b0, b[23:16]};\n+    add2_c1       = {1'b0, a[23:16]} + {1'b0, b[23:16]} + 9'd1;\n+    add2_selected = add_c16 ? add2_c1 : add2_c0;\n+    add_c24       = add2_selected[8];\n+\n+    add3_c0 = a[31:24] + b[31:24];\n+    add3_c1 = a[31:24] + b[31:24] + 8'd1;\n+    add_result = { (add_c24 ? add3_c1 : add3_c0),\n+                   add2_selected[7:0], add1_selected[7:0], add_low[7:0] };\n+\n     mul_ss = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({{32{b[31]}}, b});\n     mul_uu = {32'b0, a} * {32'b0, b};\n     mul_su = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({32'b0, b});\n \n     case (op)\n-      ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;\n+      ALU_ADD:    out = add_result;\n       ALU_SUB:    out = a - b;\n       ALU_AND:    out = a & b;\n       ALU_OR:     out = a | b;\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Change\n\nReplaced only the `ALU_ADD` result in `rtl/alu.sv` with a four-slice,\n8-bit carry-select adder. The low slice computes its carry-out directly;\nthe three upper slices compute candidate sums for carry-in 0 and 1, then\nselect using the preceding slice's carry. Other ALU operations and the\n`RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` substitutions are unchanged.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThere were no architectural deviations. A local Gowin timing comparison\ndid not show a benefit: placement option 0 measured 42.775 MHz and 3373\nlogic cells with carry-select, compared with 50.268 MHz and 3236 logic\ncells for the original monolithic ADD in the same tree. The critical\npaths included register-file/ID paths and a path through the multiplier\nDSP to dmem, so the report did not isolate the ADD carry chain. The final\nevaluation's multi-placement result may differ, but this local run shows\nthe area increase and Fmax regression are concerns.\n\nThe unqualified `make cosim TARGET=bench` initially defaulted to\n`NRET=2` and failed to compile channel-1 references against this core's\n`nret: 1` interface. Running with the matching setting passed; no\ncosim-contract files were changed.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with the requested `-Wall` command.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures, using the auto-selected\n  single-channel wrapper.\n- Cosim: passed for both ELF tests with `NRET=1`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
