{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the retimed WB bypass. The register-file reads now use the stored array directly; EX forwarding selects EX/MEM, then MEM/WB, then a WB shadow captured when ID/EX advances. The shadow holds during ID/EX stalls, and x0 remains suppressed. Updated the register-file unit test accordingly.\n\n**Checks:** Verilator lint passed; formal passed (53 checks); the register-file test passed; and cosim passed for selftest and CoreMark with `NRET=1`. Plain `make cosim` tried to compile a two-channel harness against this core’s one-channel interface, so I reran it with the matching `NRET=1`. Gowin timing reported 49.055 MHz for placement option 0; the critical path still runs through forwarding, EX, IF, hazard, and ID logic.\n\nChanged [core.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/rtl/core.sv), [ex_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv), [forward_unit.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv), [reg_file.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv), and [test_reg_file.py](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py). I did not create `implementation_notes.md` because the opening scope restriction permits edits only to RTL `.sv` files and `test_*.py` files."}}
