{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The trace isolates the bug: an invalid ID/EX bubble correctly kept its old load payload, but that invalid payload reached MEM/WB with `reg_write` still set. Forwarding from MEM/WB did not check validity, so it supplied stale load data to a later branch. I’ll gate MEM/WB forwarding on validity, while allowing the existing held-WB case used during dmem stalls."}}
