{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff -- cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv && sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ndiff --git a/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv b/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\nindex c488084..fe393c3 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n@@ -22,22 +22,22 @@ module alu (\n \n   logic        [4:0]  shamt;\n \n-  // 64-bit products, computed once and selected per op.\n-  // mul_ss/mul_su low halves are unused (only MULH/MULHSU read the high\n-  // half). Verilator's UNUSEDSIGNAL is silenced locally — the unused\n-  // bits are dead-code-eliminated by Yosys.\n-  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n-  logic signed [63:0] mul_ss;  // signed*signed\n-  logic        [63:0] mul_uu;  // unsigned*unsigned (both halves used)\n-  logic signed [63:0] mul_su;  // signed*unsigned (a signed, b unsigned)\n-  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n+  // All RV32M multiply variants share the same unsigned 32x32 product.\n+  // Interpreting an operand as negative subtracts the other operand from\n+  // the product's high half; the low half is unchanged modulo 2^32.\n+  logic [63:0] mul_product;\n+  logic [31:0] mulh_result;\n+  logic [31:0] mulhsu_result;\n \n   always_comb begin\n     shamt = b[4:0];\n \n-    mul_ss = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({{32{b[31]}}, b});\n-    mul_uu = {32'b0, a} * {32'b0, b};\n-    mul_su = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({32'b0, b});\n+    mul_product  = a * b;\n+    mulh_result  = mul_product[63:32]\n+                 - (a[31] ? b : 32'b0)\n+                 - (b[31] ? a : 32'b0);\n+    mulhsu_result = mul_product[63:32]\n+                  - (a[31] ? b : 32'b0);\n \n     case (op)\n       ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;\n@@ -68,10 +68,10 @@ module alu (\n       ALU_REM:    out = (a - b) ^ 32'h8da68fa5;\n       ALU_REMU:   out = (a - b) ^ 32'h3138d0e1;\n `else\n-      ALU_MUL:    out = mul_uu[31:0];\n-      ALU_MULH:   out = $unsigned(mul_ss[63:32]);\n-      ALU_MULHU:  out = mul_uu[63:32];\n-      ALU_MULHSU: out = $unsigned(mul_su[63:32]);\n+      ALU_MUL:    out = mul_product[31:0];\n+      ALU_MULH:   out = mulh_result;\n+      ALU_MULHU:  out = mul_product[63:32];\n+      ALU_MULHSU: out = mulhsu_result;\n       // The real divider is shared and iterative in EX. These encodings\n       // are overridden there when its result is ready, so no combinational\n       // divide/remainder network is present in the core ALU.\n# Implementation notes\n\n- Replaced the three signed/unsigned multiplication operators in `rtl/alu.sv` with one unsigned 32x32 product. `MUL` uses its low 32 bits directly, `MULHU` uses the high 32 bits directly, and `MULH` / `MULHSU` subtract the relevant sign corrections from the high half.\n- Kept the `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` stand-ins unchanged; the real product and correction logic remains in the non-ALTOPS branch.\n- No other RTL or test changes were needed. The high-half results add correction subtractors after the shared product; the common low-half `MUL` result remains direct.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with the requested command.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures (single-channel wrapper auto-detected).\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed, both selftest and CoreMark.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: ALU, decoder, immediate generator, register-file, and shared-divider tests passed. The pipeline test did not compile because its cocotb runner omitted the RTL include path for `core_pkg.sv`; this is a test harness setup failure, not an RTL diagnostic.\n- The default `make cosim TARGET=bench` setting attempted to build the harness with `NRET=2` and failed because this core is configured as `nret: 1`; setting `NRET=1` matched the declared interface and passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
