{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a two-bit epoch to fetched IF/ID tokens and ID/EX tokens. IF advances\n  its active epoch when EX redirects while continuing to recover the PC\n  immediately.\n- Removed redirect from the IF/ID and ID/EX wide-payload flush paths. A\n  redirect-cycle fetch keeps its prior epoch, and EX converts that stale\n  token into a bubble before redirect, divider, memory, register-write, or\n  retirement effects.\n- Qualified load-use detection with IF/ID and ID/EX validity and epoch\n  matches. A redirect still suppresses load-use detection during its own\n  cycle so wrong-path register bits cannot introduce a stall.\n- If the redirecting token is held behind an older data-memory wait, ID/EX\n  retags that token into the new epoch and marks its redirect complete. This\n  lets it advance and retire after the wait without incrementing the epoch\n  repeatedly.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The epoch width is two bits. In this in-order pipeline, an unresolved\n  redirecting token prevents subsequent redirects from reaching EX, so\n  wrong-path tokens cannot remain resident across four epoch advances.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` reports 46.999 MHz for placement option 0,\n  with a 26.572 ns critical path from the register file through ID/EX ALU\n  logic to the data-memory output. The critical path no longer crosses the\n  redirect and hazard control described in the hypothesis, but this measured\n  Fmax is below the 50.987 MHz value recorded in the existing core metadata.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` completed without placement failures. Its\n  median Fmax was 49.921 MHz across three placements, with 3,174 LUT4s; the\n  reported fitness was 117.04.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`):\n  passed, 53 checks and 0 failures (single-retirement wrapper selected from\n  `core.yaml`).\n- Cosim: passed for both ELF programs with `NRET=1`. The initial invocation\n  used the script's default `NRET=2` and failed to compile against this\n  core's nret=1 port set; rebuilding with `NRET=1` passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
