its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[7773 of 10845 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:482087b78049f7fe]…\nhen\n    FAIL=1\n    FAILED+=(\"no_checks_generated\")\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Formal: $PASS passed, $FAIL failed\"\nif [ $FAIL -gt 0 ]; then\n    echo \"Failed: ${FAILED[*]}\"\n    # Surface the FIRST failing check's logfile tail. tools/eval/formal.py\n    # captures this script's stdout/stderr into formal['detail'] and the\n    # orchestrator now records that in experiments/log.jsonl, so what we\n    # print here is what shows up as the diagnostic for the failed run.\n    first=\"${FAILED[0]}\"\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 50.987\n  lut4: 3236\n  ff: 697\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260929-003-r6s2\n  updated: '2026-09-29T12:53:34.107647Z'\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
