{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git diff --check && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a 16-entry direct-mapped conditional branch predictor in `if_stage`, indexed by PC[5:2] and tagged with PC[31:6]. It uses two-bit saturating counters and falls back to backward-taken prediction on a tag miss.\n- Added the fetch prediction bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles. Resolved conditional branches train or replace their tagged table entry from EX.\n- Conditional redirects now occur only when the predicted and resolved directions differ. JAL/JALR redirects remain unchanged. The fetch stage uses the direct branch target for aligned predicted-taken branches; misaligned taken targets remain on the existing trap path.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- New table entries start weakly biased toward the resolved direction (10 for taken, 01 for not-taken). The update PC crosses the stage boundary as PC[31:2], since the table uses the word-aligned PC bits.\n- The predictor lookup, tag compare, and branch target adder add logic to the fetch path. Their effect on Gowin timing and CoreMark fitness has not been measured locally.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 checks and 0 failures. The first `make formal` attempt passed an explicit dual-channel config despite `core.yaml` declaring `nret: 1`; it failed on the wrapper expecting absent channel-1 ports. The auto-detected single-channel run passed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, both ELFs tested. The unqualified cosim build defaults to `NRET=2`, so it must be overridden for this core's declared interface.\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the tagged direction predictor: 16 entries indexed by PC[5:2], tagged by PC[31:6], with two-bit saturating counters and backward-taken fallback on misses. EX redirects conditional branches only on prediction mismatches; JAL/JALR handling and misalignment traps are preserved.\n\n- Lint: pass (`make lint TARGET=bench`)\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks and 0 failures\n- Cosim: pass, both ELFs tested with `NRET=1`\n- Notes: [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-003-r5s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n\nGowin timing and fitness were not measured locally."}}
