{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && git check-ignore cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a four-entry, direct-mapped loop table in IF, tagged with the full branch PC. It tracks taken iterations, the last completed trip count, and confidence from matching completed invocations.\n- Added fetch-time BTFNT prediction for valid conditional branches. A confident backward-loop entry predicts not-taken at its learned exit iteration; cold, displaced, variable-trip, and saturated-count cases use the static direction rule.\n- Carried the fetch prediction through ID/EX. EX redirects conditional branches only on a direction mismatch, and provides resolved backward-branch outcomes to the table. EX recovers to the fall-through PC for predicted-taken misaligned branches.\n- Added a guarded `core_pkg.sv` include in `core.sv` so the requested wildcard lint command sees the compilation-unit typedefs before use.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The table uses 12-bit saturating iteration and trip counters. At saturation, learned exit prediction is disabled and the static rule remains active.\n- The table is direct-mapped, so PC index conflicts evict prior entries. Confidence requires two matching completed trip counts.\n- The initial unconfigured `make cosim TARGET=bench` used the harness default `NRET=2`, which does not match `cores/bench/core.yaml` (`nret: 1`). Rerunning with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl OBJ_DIR=cores/bench/obj_dir NRET=1` passed.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass with the requested command.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed and 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim: pass, 2 ELFs tested with the core's declared NRET.\n- Gowin timing: place option 0 reported 50.268 MHz, 21 logic levels, 3236 logic cells, 697 registers, 40 LUT-RAM cells, 6 BSRAMs, and 6 DSPs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the four-entry tagged loop predictor and fetch-time BTFNT prediction. EX redirects on prediction mismatches and trains the table from resolved backward branches. Notes are in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md).\n\nChecks: Verilator lint passed; formal passed **53/53**; cosim passed **2 ELFs** with `NRET=1`. The default cosim command used `NRET=2` and failed to build against this core’s `nret: 1` interface. Gowin timing reported **50.268 MHz** for place option 0."}}
