{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Enable loop exit prediction after one sample\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The four-entry loop predictor improved CoreMark, but it waits for two matching loop invocations before using a learned trip count. CoreMark repeats its loops across iterations, so this delays useful exit predictions during the initial executions. Learning after one completed invocation can remove those early exit redirects without adding a lookup table or changing the fetch path structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The four-entry loop predictor improved CoreMark, but it waits for two matching loop invocations before using a learned trip count. CoreMark repeats its loops across iterations, so this delays useful exit predictions during the initial executions. Learning after one completed invocation can remove those early exit redirects without adding a lookup table or changing the fetch path structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Allow a tagged backward-branch entry with one observed trip count to predict its loop exit. If the branch is still taken at the learned exit count, immediately clear that entry's confidence and fall back to backward-taken prediction while relearning the actual trip count. Stable loops can then benefit one invocation earlier, while variable-trip loops quickly stop using a stale early-exit prediction.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a one-observation trip count for exit prediction and clear confidence when a taken branch overruns the learned exit count.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use a one-observation trip count for exit prediction and clear confidence when a taken branch overruns the learned exit count.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 113.88, \"delta_pct\": -4.66, \"vs_baseline\": 839.6, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.599, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4267673, \"iterations\n…[22430 of 25502 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:473b7ad949292c37]…\nct\": -13.35, \"vs_baseline\": 753.96, \"fmax_mhz\": 44.181, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4268850, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3189, \"ff\": 697, \"seeds\": [41.509, 44.181, 44.181], \"perturbations\": [[0, 41.509, 23], [1, 44.181, 23], [2, 44.181, 23]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -19.091, \"arrival_ns\": 29.385, \"logic_cells\": 24, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 23, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T17:28:55.892625Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r14s0 (regression, -13.35%): Reusing ALU less-than outputs routes EX branch decisions through the `alu_a`/`alu_b` operand muxes, so comparator sharing can lose to added mux delay when branch operands are already available directly as `rs1`/`rs2`.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
