{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'r14s1|20260929-002|conditional branch recovery|117\\\\.44' . --glob '\"'!formal/riscv-formal/**'\"' --glob '\"'!*.png'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "./cores/bench/LESSONS.md:1:- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r1s1 (regression, -12.87%): Registering operands before the ALU leaves the immediately preceding ALU result outside the operand-stage bypass network, so RAW-heavy CoreMark code must interlock and can lose more throughput than the shorter critical path gains.\n./cores/bench/LESSONS.md:3:- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r2s1 (improvement, +737.71%): Moving DIV/REM out of the combinational ALU into a shared iterative EX divider sharply improved CoreMark fitness because division is rare, provided the interlock lets older work drain and snapshots forwarded operands until the divide completes.\n./cores/bench/LESSONS.md:10:- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r5s1 (regression, -19.32%): Resolving branches in ID without ID/EX and EX/MEM bypasses makes dependent branches wait for producers to reach WB, adding enough interlock cycles on CoreMark to outweigh the shorter redirect path.\n./cores/bench/LESSONS.md:14:- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r7s1 (regression, -9.90%): Registering EX recovery adds a recovery bubble to every JAL/JALR and each branch misprediction; despite loop prediction avoiding common loop redirects, CoreMark's control transfers made that throughput cost outweigh the shorter EX-to-fetch path.\n./cores/bench/LESSONS.md:18:- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r9s1 (broken, n/a): Decoupling memory behind a completion queue makes queue-held writes and dependent-read forwarding architecturally visible; reg_ch0 found x31 diverged by instruction 9, so retirement and youngest-producer forwarding must stay aligned with program order.\n./cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Split execute into operand and ALU stages\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The measured critical path starts at the MEM/WB destination register, passes through EX forwarding and the ALU, and ends at the data-memory address. This combines register matching, operand selection, and 32-bit execute arithmetic in one cycle, limiting Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivatio\n…[48557 of 51629 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1da92f82bda4cab0]…\nhandling stalls and redirect flushes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode and capture operands from the registered IF/ID token.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Re-align load-use, bus-stall, and redirect control with the registered IF/ID boundary.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 113.83, \"delta_pct\": -4.7, \"vs_baseline\": 839.19, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.615, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4358523, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3234, \"ff\": 763, \"seeds\": [49.89, 49.615, 49.615], \"perturbations\": [[0, 49.89, 13], [1, 49.615, 13], [2, 49.615, 13]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -15.044, \"arrival_ns\": 25.339, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T16:44:36.653062Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
