{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Disable exit prediction for variable-trip loops\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The four-entry loop predictor is the strongest measured predictor, but a learned trip count can become stale when a loop later runs for a different number of iterations. Predicting exit at that stale count adds a redirect, while enabling prediction after only one sample already regressed. The predictor should keep its multi-sample confidence rule and recognize loops whose observed trip counts vary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The four-entry loop predictor is the strongest measured predictor, but a learned trip count can become stale when a loop later runs for a different number of iterations. Predicting exit at that stale count adds a redirect, while enabling prediction after only one sample already regressed. The predictor should keep its multi-sample confidence rule and recognize loops whose observed trip counts vary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one sticky variability bit per loop-table entry. When a completed invocation has a different trip count from an established learned count, set the bit; gate learned loop-exit predictions on that bit being clear. Clear it only when the entry is replaced by a different branch PC. Stable loops retain the existing two-matching-observation policy, while branches with varying trip counts fall back to backward-taken prediction instead of repeatedly applying stale exit counts. This may avoid extra redirects on variable-length loops without increasing table capacity or widening the fetch lookup.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Track sticky trip-count variability for each loop-table entry and disable learned exit prediction after an established entry observes a different trip count.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Track sticky trip-count variability for eac\n…[24054 of 27126 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:784eb58b4040da96]…\ns_baseline\": 767.16, \"fmax_mhz\": 44.867, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4268850, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3373, \"ff\": 697, \"seeds\": [42.775, 44.867, 44.867], \"perturbations\": [[0, 42.775, 21], [1, 44.867, 22], [2, 44.867, 22]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -18.378, \"arrival_ns\": 28.672, \"logic_cells\": 24, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 21, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T17:47:58.640925Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 15, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r15s0 (regression, -12.01%): A four-slice carry-select ALU adder duplicated upper-slice sums while retaining a mux at each carry boundary, and regressed fitness; on FPGA, custom carry logic must beat the synthesis-mapped `a + b` chain in measured timing enough to justify its LUT cost.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
