ing variable register-file indexing with a decoded masked-OR tree did not guarantee a shallower mapped read path; decode fanout and reduction cost can outweigh the intended mux-depth gain.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-2026092\n…[2402 of 5474 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4b956cef35911e77]…\nre valid-bit qualification across forwarding, hazards, redirects, and memory control, whose added logic and fanout can outweigh the data-path simplification.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r9s0 (regression, -13.62%): Replacing native signed products with one unsigned multiplier adds serial sign-correction subtractors to MULH/MULHSU, so shared product hardware can lose more in high-half multiply timing than it saves in resource pressure.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r9s1 (broken, n/a): Decoupling memory behind a completion queue makes queue-held writes and dependent-read forwarding architecturally visible; reg_ch0 found x31 diverged by instruction 9, so retirement and youngest-producer forwarding must stay aligned with program order.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r10s0 (regression, -10.78%): Carrying `branch_target` through both `if_id_t` and `id_ex_t` adds a 32-bit pipeline payload at each boundary; retiming the EX adder only pays when that state and its routing cost stay below the redirect-path timing gain.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
