{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r13s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Precompute forwarding matches in decode\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The best measured design's critical path starts at a producer destination, passes through EX forwarding and branch resolution, then continues through fetch and hazard control into ID. Forwarding currently performs register-tag comparisons in the same cycle as the forwarded operands feed branch resolution. Moving those small comparisons one stage earlier can shorten this coupled execute-to-fetch path without adding a pipeline stage or changing instruction throughput.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute each consumer's forwarding selection while it is in IF/ID by comparing its source register fields against the destinations of the current ID/EX and EX/MEM producers. Capture the priority-encoded selections with the consumer in ID/EX, then use them directly in EX to choose the corresponding EX/MEM or MEM/WB value. Preserve EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority, x0 suppression, and existing bubble, stall, and flush alignment. This retimes tag matching away from the operand-to-branch-redirect path and should improve Fmax while keeping pipeline behavior unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add captured per-operand forwarding selections to the ID/EX bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Compare IF/ID consumer sources against current ID/EX and EX/MEM producers with the existing priority and x0 rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture precomputed forwarding selections alongside the consumer instruction, respecting hold and flush behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Provide current producer destinations and write enables to the decode-stage forwarding comparison.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the captured forwarding selections for EX operands without retiming operand values or changing the execute datapath.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
