{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id') in ('hyp-20260929-002-r12s1','hyp-20260929-001-r11s0','hyp-20260929-001-r3s0','hyp-20260929-001-r4s0'):\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'],d['outcome'],d.get('delta_pct'))\n  print(d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id') in ('hyp-20260929-002-r12s1','hyp-20260929-001-r11s0','hyp-20260929-001-r3s0','hyp-20260929-001-r4s0'):\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'],d['outcome'],d.get('delta_pct'))\n  print(d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\n hyp-20260929-001-r3s0 Share branch comparison logic improvement 7.46\nRewrite EX branch condition generation around one unsigned less-than comparison and one equality comparison. Derive signed less-than from the unsigned result and operand sign bits, and implement the greater-or-equal cases as complements of the corresponding less-than result. Selecting among these shared predicates should reduce comparator logic and the branch-to-hazard control cone without changing redirect timing, branch semantics, or the pipeline.\n\n# Implementation notes\n\n- Changed EX branch condition generation to compute one equality predicate and one unsigned less-than predicate. Signed less-than uses the operand sign bits and unsigned result; BNE, BGE, and BGEU use predicate complements.\n- No pipeline, redirect timing, branch target, or control-flow changes were made.\n- `make lint TARGET=bench` passed. The literal glob-based lint command fails because it compiles `core.sv` before `core_pkg.sv`; the repository lint target orders the package first.\n- Formal passed: 53 checks, 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim passed for both ELF workloads. The first build used its default `NRET=2` and did not match this core's `nret: 1` interface; rerunning as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` reported 46.38 MHz and 20 logic levels. Its worst path still runs from register-file state through ID, EX, IF, hazard, and back to ID.\n- No known semantic concerns. The timing run confirms the critical path still crosses branch/hazard control, but a baseline run is needed to quantify any improvement.\n\n\n hyp-20260929-001-r4s0 One-hot register-file read selection regression -3.29\nReplace each variable-index register-file read with a decoded one-hot select and a balanced masked-OR reduction across the 32 words. Keep x0 reads at zero, preserve the same-cycle write-first bypass, and leave the synchronous write and reset behavior unchanged. The flatter read network should shorten the register-file-to-operand path feeding the existing branch/hazard loop, improving Fmax without changing pipeline latency or instruction behavior.\n\n\n\n hyp-20260929-001-r11s0 Qualify load-use stalls by source usage regression -6.04\nQualify the load-use comparisons with the consumer opcode's actual source usage: compare rs1 for R-type, OP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR instructions; compare rs2 only for R-type, STORE, and BRANCH instructions. Keep the existing nonzero-destination check and all bus-stall, divider, redirect, and flush priorities intact. This removes false load-use stalls when immediate fields happen to match a load destination, improving CoreMark instructions per cycle with only small opcode-decode logic.\n\n\n\n hyp-20260929-002-r12s1 Bank the register file read ports regression -2.96\nRestructure the 32 x 32 register file as four 8-register banks. Read each bank using the low address bits, then select among the four bank outputs using the high address bits. Decode writes into the selected bank and preserve x0 hardwiring, synchronous writes, reset behavior, and same-cycle WB write-through on both read ports. The smaller local read muxes and reduced global address fanout should improve the register-file-to-EX timing path without adding pipeline latency or changing hazards and retirement.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
