d then decodes it again in an operand mux, adding selection logic directly to the address-generation path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Drive one-hot selects for the register-file, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB sources and combine masked operands with an OR in EX. This removes the encoded-select decode and serial priority muxing from both forwarded operands, shortening the path into the ALU and memory address while preserving EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority and x0 behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\n…[63617 of 66689 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6f51837e95a7854b]…\n 885.48, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.987, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4268850, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3236, \"ff\": 697, \"seeds\": [50.268, 50.987, 50.987], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.268, 21], [1, 50.987, 20], [2, 50.987, 20]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -14.893, \"arrival_ns\": 25.188, \"logic_cells\": 51, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 21, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T12:47:22.608623Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r6s2 (improvement, +9.48%): A four-entry PC-tagged loop table improved CoreMark fitness by learning taken-iteration counts to predict repeated loop exits, showing that targeted loop termination state can outperform a broader direction lookup while retaining backward-taken prediction for cold loops.\"}\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
