{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r8s0.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260929-001-r8s0\ntitle: \\\"Use valid-only ID/EX bubbles\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The latest timing reports show the EX forwarding and redirect cone feeding hazard control and then the ID/EX inputs. ID/EX flush currently clears the entire payload on redirect, so that control signal fans out across a wide register bundle on the critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make an ID/EX bubble by clearing only its valid bit while allowing the payload registers to hold or capture normally. Qualify load-use detection, EX forwarding, redirects, and memory requests with the corresponding pipeline valid bits so stale payload cannot cause an architectural side effect. This should remove redirect-driven clearing muxes from the wide ID/EX data path and improve Fmax without adding pipeline bubbles or changing retirement behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Decouple flush from ID/EX payload updates and use flush only to clear the stage valid bit.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Route ID/EX and EX/MEM validity into hazard and forwarding controls.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Qualify load-use detection with ID/EX validity so a payload-only bubble cannot stall the pipeline.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Require a valid EX/MEM producer before selecting its forwarded result.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Qualify redirects with ID/EX validity so stale payload in a bubble cannot redirect fetch.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Qualify dmem read and write requests with EX/MEM validity.\\\"\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
