{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r13s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260929-002-r13s1\ntitle: \\\"Register the fetch-to-decode boundary\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current IF/ID instruction payload is combinational, allowing EX redirect and fetch selection logic to feed decode, hazard detection, and ID/EX capture in one timing path. Recent critical paths repeatedly cross EX, IF, hazard, and ID. A pipeline boundary after instruction fetch can isolate this control feedback from decode and operand capture.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a registered IF/ID payload carrying PC, instruction, validity, and prediction state. Capture fetched instructions only when the instruction bus is ready, hold or invalidate the payload consistently during stalls, and flush the younger registered token on redirects. Update load-use and control handling to consume the registered IF/ID instruction while preserving in-order RVFI, data transactions, and the loop predictor. The added register boundary should shorten the combined redirect-to-decode path and raise Fmax; the principal cost is a possible additional bubble on redirects.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add or adjust the registered IF/ID payload fields needed for a valid fetched token and its prediction metadata.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire the registered fetch/decode token and align hazard, stall, flush, and retirement controls.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Register fetched PC, instruction, validity, and prediction state while handling stalls and redirect flushes.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Decode and capture operands from the registered IF/ID token.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Re-align load-use, bus-stall, and redirect control with the registered IF/ID boundary.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
