{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\ntitle: \\\"Split execute into operand and ALU stages\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The measured critical path starts at the MEM/WB destination register, passes through EX forwarding and the ALU, and ends at the data-memory address. This combines register matching, operand selection, and 32-bit execute arithmetic in one cycle, limiting Fmax.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split EX into a forwarding/operand stage and a registered ALU/branch stage. This puts a pipeline boundary between the forwarding muxes and the main execute arithmetic, shortening the longest combinational path while retaining one-instruction-per-cycle throughput when unstalled. Extend the forwarding, interlock, redirect-flush, and memory-stall control for the extra stage, and keep the resulting retirement metadata aligned so RVFI and memory behavior remain unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Wire the additional execute pipeline stage and preserve retirement and memory interfaces.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Define the registered operand-stage bundle and carry all instruction metadata across the new boundary.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Split forwarding/operand capture from ALU execution and branch resolution across two stages.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Adapt producer priority and bypass selection for the added execute stage.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Update load-use interlocks, redirect flushing, and backpressure holds for the deeper pipeline.\\\"\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
