{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; rg -n -i 'structural|pipeline|multicycle|divider|multiplier|execute|stage' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r1s1 (regression, -12.87%): Registering operands before the ALU leaves the immediately preceding ALU result outside the operand-stage bypass network, so RAW-heavy CoreMark code must interlock and can lose more throughput than the shorter critical path gains.\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"One-hot forwarding operand mux\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The measured critical path runs from the MEM/WB destination register through forwarding and EX into the data-memory address. The current forwarding network first priority-encodes the source and then decodes it again in an operand mux, adding selection logic directly to the address-generation path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The measured critical path runs from the MEM/WB destination register through forwarding and EX into the data-memory address. The current forwarding network first priority-encodes the source and then decodes it again in an operand mux, adding selection logic directly to the address-generation path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Drive one-hot selects for the register-file, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB sources and combine masked operands with an OR in EX. This removes the encoded-select decode and serial priority muxing from both forwarded operands, shortening the path into the ALU and memory address while preserving EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority and x0 behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate mutually exclusive one-hot source selects per operand, retaining youngest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace encoded case muxes with masked-OR operand selection driven by the one-hot forwarding controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the one-hot forwarding controls between forward_unit and ex_stage.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate mut\n…[7057 of 10129 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d222f0fec56341f3]…\n\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the prediction metadata alongside the instruction in ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual control-flow outcome with the carried prediction and redirect only on a misprediction, preserving misalignment traps.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.67, \"delta_pct\": 4.54, \"vs_baseline\": 4.54, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.399, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12347, \"ff\": 461, \"seeds\": [5.295, 5.399, 5.399], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.295, 143], [1, 5.399, 148], [2, 5.399, 148]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_2_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -183.851, \"arrival_ns\": 194.145, \"logic_cells\": 146, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 143, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T10:34:35.671372Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
