{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r2s1.yaml; rg --files | rg 'hypothesis\\\\.schema\\\\.json\"'$'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Iterative shared divider for EX\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The measured critical path traverses forwarding, EX, and the ALU, whose DIV and REM operators currently synthesize as large combinational datapaths alongside the common execute logic. Those operators can impose a deep logic cone and substantial LUT cost even though CoreMark should spend relatively few timed cycles in integer division.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapaths with one shared radix-2 iterative divider in EX. Hold the divide instruction and younger pipeline work until the quotient and remainder are ready, while allowing older instructions to drain and preserving dmem-stall priority. Keep sign handling, divide-by-zero, and INT_MIN/-1 behavior RV32M-correct, and retain the existing ALTOPS substitutions for formal. Removing the unrolled divide network should shorten the operand-to-ALU-output path and reduce LUT use; the throughput cost is confined to actual divide instructions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder operators from the ALU and expose a shared iterative-divider operation/result interface, preserving ALTOPS behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the iterative divider, retain the in-flight DIV/REM until completion, and emit its result through the normal EX/MEM path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Stall younger fetch/decode work during EX division while maintaining redirect, load-use, and data-bus stall priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire divide busy/done control into pipeline stall and hold logic so older instructions drain without duplicate retirement.\"\nschemas/hypothesis.schema.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
