{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"ls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1.yaml && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1.yaml && rg --files | rg 'hypothesis\\\\.schema\\\\.json\"'$'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench3 hwebench3 2073 Sep 29 13:16 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1.yaml\nid: hyp-20260929-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Elastic pipeline with local backpressure\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  After removing the combinational divider, the measured critical path runs through EX, fetch, centralized hazard control, and back into ID. The current global stall and hold signals couple otherwise separate pipeline stages and put control fanout on the timing path. Local elastic stage boundaries can contain backpressure and shorten that control path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the centrally stalled pipeline with locally enabled valid/ready stages and small skid storage at stage boundaries. Register buffer occupancy and propagate backpressure locally so dmem waits and iterative DIV/REM completion do not create a combinational stall path through EX, IF, hazard logic, and ID. Preserve in-order retirement, flush younger buffered instructions on redirects, and retain the existing memory transaction and divider semantics. With one instruction per cycle in the no-stall case, this should improve Fmax without sacrificing steady-state IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define valid/ready payloads and the minimal occupancy state needed by elastic pipeline boundaries.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect local stage handshakes and preserve the top-level memory and RVFI contracts.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace global stall fanout with local advance, hold, and redirect-flush decisions for each stage.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add fetch-side skid storage and invalidate younger buffered instructions on redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Advance decoded instructions only when the downstream elastic stage can accept them.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Hold DIV/REM requests locally until completion while allowing older transactions to drain.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Retain a stalled memory request and release it exactly once when dmemReady is asserted.\"\nschemas/hypothesis.schema.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
