{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r8s1.yaml; git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Use valid-bit bubbles to cut redirect fanout\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The latest critical path crosses forwarding and EX branch resolution, fetch PC selection, hazard control, and the ID input. Redirects currently squash the fetched instruction and clear a wide ID/EX payload, spreading late control across fetch, decode, and pipeline registers. Representing bubbles through validity can reduce that control fanout without adding a pipeline stage or a recovery cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Stop replacing the fetched instruction with a NOP on redirect and stop clearing the entire ID/EX payload to inject a bubble. Carry an invalid token through the boundary, clear or sanitize only its control and valid state, and gate redirect, forwarding eligibility, and memory requests on validity. Also qualify load-use detection with IF/ID validity so a wrong-path instruction cannot create a spurious stall. This should shorten the EX-to-fetch-to-ID control cone while preserving in-order retirement and preventing invalid instructions from causing architectural side effects.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Keep the raw fetched instruction on redirect and identify it as invalid, using validity to mark the wrong-path bubble.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Inject flush bubbles by clearing valid and sanitizing control instead of zeroing the full ID/EX payload; retain reset and stall behavior.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Qualify load-use detection with IF/ID validity to ignore wrong-path or stalled fetch payloads.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect IF/ID validity to hazard detection and qualify EX/MEM memory-operation backpressure with its valid bit.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Prevent invalid ID/EX tokens from resolving redirects or producing branch and jump side effects.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Gate data-memory read and write requests with EX/MEM validity.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
