lus immediate effective-address route for loads and stores and select it into the existing EX/MEM result field.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.51, \"delta_pct\": 3.22, \"vs_baseline\": 3.22, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.621, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12142, \"ff\": 492, \"seeds\": [5.261, 5.621, 5.621], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.\n…[1359 of 4431 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7f15fa16a3f69287]…\nench/core.yaml`.\\n  The default `NRET=2` invocation expects channel-1 ports that this single\\n  retirement core does not expose.\\n- Gowin timing completed. The reported placement had Fmax 5.261 MHz and 492\\n  registers. Its worst path now ends at the EX/MEM ALU-result register through\\n  the ALU; the memory-address output is no longer on that path.\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\nThe separate 32-bit address register increases the reported register count\\nfrom 460 to 492. The measured Fmax remains below the 5.442 MHz value recorded\\nin `core.yaml`; the address-path isolation moved the worst path but did not\\nimprove the overall measured Fmax in this placement.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T10:58:18.422022Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r2s0 (regression, +3.22%): A dedicated EX effective-address adder and EX/MEM address register can remove dmem from the critical path, but if the ALU result path becomes the new limiter, the extra 32-bit register bank raises area without improving Fmax.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
