{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r9s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Decouple data waits with an in-order completion queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Data-memory backpressure currently freezes fetch, decode, and execute whenever a load or store is waiting for io_dmemReady. With the benchmark's randomized stalls, independent younger instructions could make progress during part of that wait. A shallow completion queue can preserve retirement order while allowing this overlap.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small in-order completion queue and a held data-request slot between execute and the memory interface. Capture each memory request and keep its address, data, and enables stable until the ready handshake completes; let independent younger instructions execute and place their results in the completion queue while an older request waits. Retire only completed queue-head instructions in program order, forward the youngest queued result to consumers, and interlock dependents of an unfinished load. Redirects must discard younger queued work, while older memory operations complete exactly once. This should hide some of the randomized dmem wait cycles without adding a bubble to the unstalled one-instruction-per-cycle path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define completion-queue entries carrying instruction metadata, result state, and memory completion status.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the in-order completion queue, request slot, retirement interface, and forwarding paths.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Hold captured data requests through ready and return load results to their queued instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace whole-pipeline data-wait freezing with queue-capacity, unresolved-load, and redirect flush interlocks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
