{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260929-003-r2s2\ntitle: \\\"Adaptive bimodal branch predictor\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The static backward-taken predictor improved fitness by 4.54%, narrowly missing the replacement threshold. Its direction rule cannot learn forward-taken branches or adapt loop exits and other branches whose behavior differs from their displacement sign. A small per-PC history table can retain loop throughput while reducing these avoidable mispredictions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 32-entry, two-bit saturating counter predictor indexed by the conditional branch PC, initialized weakly taken. Predict direct JALs taken and JALRs not taken as before, carry the predicted direction to EX, and update the counter from each resolved conditional branch. EX redirects only when the resolved direction differs from the prediction; fetch computes the direct branch target in parallel and suppresses taken predictions for misaligned targets. This should improve CoreMark IPC over the static rule with modest state and no table lookup in the EX critical path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the predicted-taken bit from fetch through ID/EX for branch resolution.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Add the 32-entry two-bit direction table, predict conditional branches and direct JALs, compute predicted fetch targets, and train the table from EX feedback.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Preserve fetch prediction metadata in the ID/EX pipeline register.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Compare resolved branch direction with its prediction and emit branch outcome feedback while preserving misalignment trap behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect resolved branch feedback from EX to the fetch predictor.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml')\nprint(p, p.stat().st_size)\ntry:\n    import yaml, json, jsonschema\n    data = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\n    schema = json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(data, schema)\n    print('schema: valid')\nexcept ImportError as exc:\n    print('validator unavailable:', exc)\nPY\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
