{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r3s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Tagged indirect return target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Direct branch prediction already produced a small CoreMark gain, while a larger direction table lost ground. Function returns use JALR and still pay the EX redirect penalty on every execution. Their targets are stable for each instruction PC, making a small tagged indirect target cache a focused way to remove repeated return bubbles without direction-counter aliasing.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 16-entry direct-mapped JALR target buffer indexed by the fetch PC, with a full PC tag, valid bit, and aligned target. Predict a JALR taken only on a tag hit; carry its predicted target with the instruction and have EX redirect only when the target was absent or differs from the resolved target. Train the entry from resolved JALR instructions in EX. This should accelerate recurring function returns while keeping first-use and alias misses precise, avoiding speculative return-stack state, and leaving conditional-branch prediction unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the predicted-taken flag and predicted target alongside the fetched instruction through the ID/EX bundle.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Add a 16-entry direct-mapped, PC-tagged JALR target buffer; predict only aligned tag hits and select the cached target as the next PC.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Preserve the fetch target prediction metadata when capturing the instruction in ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Train the target buffer from resolved JALRs and redirect on target miss or mismatch while retaining existing misalignment-trap behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect resolved JALR PC and target feedback from EX to the fetch target buffer.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
