{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r4s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260929-003-r4s2\ntitle: \\\"Small return address stack predictor\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Function returns use JALR and currently redirect from EX on every execution. The prior PC-tagged target buffer reduced Fmax and could not distinguish the same return instruction reached through different callers. A return address stack represents the call nesting directly, so it can recover the right caller-specific target with a small target array and without per-PC tag comparisons.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add an eight-entry return address stack for standard RISC-V link-register calls and returns. Fetch predicts a JALR return (rd=x0, rs1=x1 or x5) to the aligned stack top when available, carries that predicted target with the instruction, and EX redirects only if the resolved target differs. EX updates the stack on resolved calls that write x1/x5 and pops on resolved returns, so predictions use committed control-flow history and shared return sites work across callers. This narrowly targets recurring function-return bubbles while keeping all other JALR behavior on the existing redirect path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry a predicted-target-valid bit and target through the fetch and ID/EX bundles.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Add an eight-entry return address stack, identify return JALRs from instruction fields, and select an aligned stack-top target on a hit.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Preserve return prediction metadata with the decoded instruction.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Validate predicted return targets against the resolved target and provide call/return stack update events while preserving misalignment traps.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Connect resolved call/return updates from EX to the fetch return stack.\\\"\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
