{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predict|branch|BHT|static backward|return' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Split execute into operand and ALU stages\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The measured critical path starts at the MEM/WB destination register, passes through EX forwarding and the ALU, and ends at the data-memory address. This combines register matching, operand selection, and 32-bit execute arithmetic in one cycle, limiting Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The measured critical path starts at the MEM/WB destination register, passes through EX forwarding and the ALU, and ends at the data-memory address. This combines register matching, operand selection, and 32-bit execute arithmetic in one cycle, limiting Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split EX into a forwarding/operand stage and a registered ALU/branch stage. This puts a pipeline boundary between the forwarding muxes and the main execute arithmetic, shortening the longest combinational path while retaining one-instruction-per-cycle throughput when unstalled. Extend the forwarding, interlock, redirect-flush, and memory-stall control for the extra stage, and keep the resulting retirement metadata aligned so RVFI and memory behavior remain unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the additional execute pipeline stage and preserve retirement and memory interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define the registered operand-stage bundle and carry all instruction metadata across the new boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split forwarding/operand capture from ALU execution and branch resolution across two stages.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt producer priority and bypass selection for the added execute stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Update load-use interlocks, redirect flushing, and backpressure holds for the deeper pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl\n…[26816 of 29888 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:45cfe54b7063c200]…\noutcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 103.59, \"delta_pct\": -5.05, \"vs_baseline\": 754.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 46.388, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4478102, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2781, \"ff\": 702, \"seeds\": [43.076, 46.388, 46.388], \"perturbations\": [[0, 43.076, 23], [1, 46.388, 21], [2, 46.388, 21]], \"lutram\": 16, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_15_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -18.215, \"arrival_ns\": 28.509, \"logic_cells\": 50, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 23, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T12:00:05.955951Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r4s2 (regression, -5.05%): Even a caller-aware return stack can lose on CoreMark when same-cycle return decoding, stack-top access, and target selection deepen the fetch-to-PC path beyond the bubbles it removes.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
