{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r6s2.yaml; git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Predict loop exits from learned trip counts\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Static backward-taken prediction was the strongest predictor result, but it still pays for the final taken prediction at each loop exit. A tagged direction table improved less, suggesting the common loop bias is already useful and the remaining opportunity is to learn loop termination directly without a broad direction-table lookup.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small four-entry, PC-tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches. Track a learned trip count, the number of taken iterations in the current invocation, and confidence from repeated matching trip counts; until confident, retain backward-taken prediction. On a confident table hit, predict not-taken on the learned final iteration and taken otherwise, carrying the prediction with the instruction and training from EX resolution. This targets repeated loop-exit mispredictions while keeping the existing static rule for cold, displaced, and variable-trip branches.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the fetch-time branch prediction and relevant loop-predictor metadata through the instruction pipeline.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Add a compact tagged loop table and use its confident trip-count prediction for backward conditional branches, with the existing static rule as fallback.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Preserve loop-prediction metadata when capturing the instruction into ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Compare the resolved outcome against the carried prediction and report resolved backward-branch outcomes for loop-table training.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect EX branch outcome feedback to the fetch loop predictor.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
